<section class="page-intro page-shell">
  <p class="eyebrow">Engineering approach</p>
  <h1>Make the work <em>inspectable.</em></h1>
  <p class="intro-lede">Tools that act around people need clear boundaries. The system should explain what it knows, what it changed, and where a person can take control.</p>
</section>

<section class="section page-shell section-tight" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
  <div class="section-heading section-heading--stacked">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Design concerns</p>
      <h2 id="principles-title">Principles that show up in the projects.</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="principle-grid">
    <article class="principle-card"><span class="principle-index">01</span><h3>Keep context durable</h3><p>Important intent, decisions, work state, and evidence should remain with the project instead of disappearing with a session.</p></article>
    <article class="principle-card"><span class="principle-index">02</span><h3>Make authority explicit</h3><p>Define who can request an action, what scope it has, and when a human decision is required.</p></article>
    <article class="principle-card"><span class="principle-index">03</span><h3>Show the evidence</h3><p>Tests and recorded outcomes should let a person review what happened and understand the limits of the result.</p></article>
    <article class="principle-card"><span class="principle-index">04</span><h3>Design for intervention</h3><p>Make errors visible and preserve the operator's ability to pause, redirect, or reject proposed work.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

